  "expected": {
    "root_cause": "config_change|deployment_correlation",
    "signals": ["config_change|deployment_correlation", "dependency_failure", "error_spike", "latency_degradation"],
    "escalate": false,
    "remediation": ["rollback_deployment"],
    "rationale": "The configuration write about ninety seconds before onset is the cause. The failing Redis target is the old cache named in the new configuration, so the dependency failure is a consequence, not an independent outage. On Container Apps a config change and a deploy are the same Activity Log operation, so a deployment-correlation finding is accepted as naming the change."
